# Spring Boot Architecture Patterns

## Project Structure

### Package Organization
```
src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/
├── controllers/          # REST controllers
├── services/            # Business logic services
├── repositories/        # Data access layer
├── dto/                 # Data Transfer Objects
├── exceptions/          # Custom exceptions
├── responses/           # API response handling
├── configuration/       # Spring configuration
├── helpers/             # Utility classes
└── rule_engine/         # Business rule processing
```

## Controller Layer

### Standard Controller Pattern
```java
@Validated
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/v1/resource")
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class ResourceController {
    
    private final IResourceService resourceService;
    private final IAPIResponder apiResponder;
    
    @PostMapping("/create")
    public ResponseEntity<?> create(@Validated @RequestBody CreateRequestDto request) {
        try {
            ResourceResponseDto result = this.resourceService.create(request);
            return this.apiResponder.respond(result, "Resource created successfully");
        }
        catch (Exception ex) {
            return this.apiResponder.respondWithError(ex, APIResponseType.ERROR, HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
        }
    }
}
```

### Response Handling
- Use [APIResponder.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/responses/APIResponder.java) for consistent responses
- Always wrap responses in `ResponseEntity<?>`
- Use try-catch blocks for exception handling
- Return structured API responses

## Service Layer

### Service Interface Pattern
```java
public interface IResourceService {
    ResourceResponseDto create(CreateRequestDto request);
    ResourceResponseDto update(Integer id, UpdateRequestDto request);
    void delete(Integer id);
}
```

### Service Implementation Pattern
```java
@Service
public class ResourceService implements IResourceService {
    
    private final IResourceRepository resourceRepository;
    private final ResourceMapper resourceMapper;
    
    @Override
    @Transactional
    public ResourceResponseDto create(CreateRequestDto request) {
        // Business logic implementation
        Resource entity = this.resourceMapper.toEntity(request);
        Resource saved = this.resourceRepository.save(entity);
        return this.resourceMapper.toDto(saved);
    }
}
```

## DTO Patterns

### Request DTOs
```java
@Data
@Builder
@NoArgsConstructor
@AllArgsConstructor
public class CreateRequestDto {
    
    @NotNull(message = "Field cannot be null")
    @Size(min = 1, max = 100, message = "Field must be between 1 and 100 characters")
    private String field;
    
    @Builder.Default
    private Boolean optionalField = false;
}
```

### Response DTOs
```java
public record ResourceResponseDto(
    Integer id,
    String name,
    String status,
    LocalDateTime createdAt
) {}
```

### Record DTOs for Simple Data
```java
public record BulkRequestDto(List<Integer> ids) {
    public BulkRequestDto {
        if (ids == null || ids.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("IDs list cannot be null or empty");
        }
    }
}
```

## Repository Layer

### JPA Repository Pattern
```java
@Repository
public interface ResourceJpaRepository extends JpaRepository<Resource, Integer> {
    
    @Query("SELECT r FROM Resource r WHERE r.accountId = :accountId")
    List<Resource> findByAccountId(@Param("accountId") Integer accountId);
    
    @EntityGraph(attributePaths = {"relatedEntity"})
    Optional<Resource> findByIdAndAccountId(Integer id, Integer accountId);
}
```

## Exception Handling

### Global Exception Handler
```java
@RestControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {
    
    @ExceptionHandler(ResourceNotFoundException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ApiResponse<?>> handleResourceNotFound(ResourceNotFoundException ex) {
        return GlobalExceptionHandler.errorResponseEntity(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND);
    }
    
    @ExceptionHandler(ValidationErrorException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ApiResponse<?>> handleValidationError(ValidationErrorException ex) {
        return GlobalExceptionHandler.errorResponseEntity(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
    }
}
```

## Dependency Injection

### Constructor Injection (Preferred)
```java
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class ServiceImpl {
    private final Repository repository;
    private final Mapper mapper;
}
```

### Field Injection (Avoid)
```java
@Service
public class ServiceImpl {
    @Autowired
    private Repository repository; // Avoid this pattern
}
```

## Transaction Management

### Service Layer Transactions
```java
@Override
@Transactional
@WriterRoute  // For write operations
public ResponseDto method(RequestDto request) {
    // Transactional business logic
}
```

## Configuration

### Application Properties
- Use [application.properties](mdc:src/main/resources/application.properties) for configuration
- Use profiles for environment-specific settings
- Externalize sensitive configuration

